      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_fe4d548b",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: america_first_when_it_comes_to_elections; hasOverallIntent: Propaganda; overall-intent-description: The image features a man in a suit speaking at a podium, with the text overlay 'america first!' at the top and 'when it comes to elections' at the bottom. The overall intent is propagandistic, aiming to associate the phrase 'America First' with the context of elections, likely to promote a nationalist or isolationist political agenda. The meme uses juxtaposition to imply that the individual or the ideology represented is prioritizing American interests above all else, especially in the context of electoral politics. There is no direct targeting of any protected group based on race, gender, religion, or other characteristics, so no toxicity is present in the form of abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynous, or discriminatory content. The intent is to influence opinion by framing 'America First' as a core principle in elections, potentially to rally support for a specific political stance or candidate.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_0366b3a7"
      },
